  message: "Option-B spirit-audit (2026-06-24) cross-refs + scope bounds, to avoid rediscovery: (1) PLAN MAPPING: INV-jifus IS the strategy doc sketch-cache family. Planned fix = sketch-cache:F1-F5 in WAVE 4 (correctness_strategy_06102026.md:194): F1 typed SketchPrecomputed contract (schema authored AGAINST THE INTROSPECTED GENERATOR; centrality respec documents BOTH zero paths; vocabulary field deleted after no-consumer re-verification); F2 substrate inversion (map-authoritative, shared loader). The strategy doc does not use the jifus name -- hence this cross-ref. (2) PREMISE REFINEMENT: the title \"no schema\" is imprecise. sketch_precomputed IS already in docs/schema.json (327-382) but as a HAND-WRITTEN overlay in generate-schema:441-477 -- NOT auto-introspected from a dataclass, no SketchPrecomputed dataclass exists, and the runtime spec_validator does NOT cover it. The real gap = no owning dataclass + hand-overlay drift risk + no per-field scope/normalization invariants. (3) PROPORTIONALITY / SCOPE BOUND: sketch_precomputed is an INTERNAL CACHE, not a wire contract -- docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:706: \"internal cache artifact -- not part of the public schema; consumers should not depend on its presence.\" All consumers internal (sketch.py reads it; compact.py strips it); zero external readers. Per the repo two-tier discipline, derived surfaces are SCHEMA-d but EXEMPT from the runtime validator (metrics/supply_chain_summary/etc.), and the ADR-0024 axis-declaration gate is scoped to ir.py/datamodels.py ONLY. So F1 = typed dataclass + introspected schema (a chokepoint), NOT full axis-governance + runtime validation -- applying the heavyweight discipline here would be over-engineering. (4) SEQUENCING: Wave 4, gated on Wave-3 (vocab axis purity feeds schema generation; file-anchor:F1 co-release). (5) NEW DOC-CONFLICT to reconcile in F1: generate-schema:296-303 comment claims sketch_precomputed \"is part of hypergumbo documented output contract\", directly contradicting spec:706 (internal cache, do not depend). Resolve these two when F1 lands."  # bce0
